witness|Observer noun and direct-object verb separated; not conflated with legal certification. Scene and opening examples preserve event details in Vietnamese, without assuming eyewitness testimony is always complete.
approximate|Estimate is distinct from actual exact cost. Definition and material-ordering example match adjective evidence; translation uses chi phí ước tính naturally and does not imply an agreed price.
honour|Five explicit source ordinals distinguish privilege, respect, public recognition, integrity and fulfilling commitments. Vietnamese mappings and objects reviewed individually; Master lemma overlap remains unresolved, never an identity claim.
merry|Cheerful atmosphere example avoids a holiday-only definition. Vietnamese voices and joint cooking stay faithful; no requirement for alcohol or one particular emotional intensity is inferred.
omit|Can be deliberate or accidental, avoiding an overly narrow forgot gloss. Address omission is a direct-object verb; Vietnamese retains room address and the note does not invent an infinitive tense rule.
